<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Flemish Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1244">1244</a>–<a href="/years/1254">1254</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Flemish Succession was a conflict over the succession to Margaret II, Countess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and Hainaut, between her sons from two marriages, the Avesnes and the Dampierre. William of Holland backed the Avesnes and defeated the Dampierre and French forces at West-Capelle in 1253. Louis IX's arbitration finally gave Flanders to the Dampierres and Hainaut to the Avesnes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-flemish-succession.jpg" alt="War of the Flemish Succession" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicod · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carte_des_comt%C3%A9s_de_Flandre_et_de_Hainaut_sous_la_comtesse_Jeanne_de_Constantinople_(1200-1244).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
